        <headline>Storm Warning issued September 24 at 4:15AM AKDT until September 24 at 5:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK</headline>
        <description>Offshore Waters Forecast for the Bering Sea

Wind forecasts reflect the predominant speed and direction
expected. Sea forecasts represent an average of the highest
one-third of the combined wind wave and swell height.

.TODAY...SE wind 35 to 50 kt becoming S 30 kt in the afternoon.
Seas
13 to 19 ft. Rain. Isolated thunderstorms.
.TONIGHT...S wind 20 to 35 kt. Seas 13 to 21 ft. Rain showers.
.FRI...SW wind 20 to 35 kt. Seas 15 to 23 ft. Rain showers.
.FRI NIGHT...W wind 20 to 30 kt. Seas 10 to 18 ft.
.SAT THROUGH MON...NW wind 10 to 25 kt. Seas 7 to 12 ft.
</description>
